ly after the opponent ran a play type heavily.", "observed_result": "Within-game change 319/523 (61.0%); cross-game change 298/440 (67.7%); 103/104 units (99.0%) and 52/52 series show a change; transition matrices near-uniform.", "auto_failure_mechanism": "A_unanswerable (question not answerable with the data or design)", "observed_failure_evidence": "Doc caveat: inferred label cannot separate real defensive adjustment from offense executing differently; near-uniform transition matrices consistent with label noise.", "observed_sample_and_power": "523 cells; 440 pairs", "auto_validation_status": "no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:label_or_classification_error"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:LABEL_ERROR"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF-APPA-001", "label": "Study family SF-APPA-001: A1 adaptation falsification: asymmetry, confidence and carryover tests", "score": 0.368, "reached_via": ["FAM:SF-APPA-005 auto_related_family (record_link_related_to) FAM:SF-APPA-001", "FAM:SF-APPA-005 auto_related_family (limitation_precedent) FAM:SF-APPA-001"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "A1 adaptation falsification: asymmetry, confidence and carryover tests", "auto_outcome_status": "artifact", "observed_hypothesis": "If the A1 adapter PPP lift is real coverage response, wrong-way teams should do worse than no-signal teams, the gap should widen with scheme-vote confidence, and adapting in Game N should carry over to Game N+1.", "observed_result": "T1 dPPP: adapter +0.0667 (n=205), neutral +0.0248 (n=50), no_signal +0.1260 (n=57), wrong_way +0.0111 (n=274). T2: adapter minus no-signal -0.0361 (1 vote), -0.1170 (2 votes). T3 next-game PPP Welch t=-1.003, p=0.842; MW [cut; read_family for the full text]", "auto_failure_mechanism": "C_artifact (apparent effect produced by a construction, selection or labelling flaw)"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:label_or_classification_error"}, {"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:selection_or_regression_to_the_mean"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:LABEL_ERROR"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:MECHANICAL_FLOOR"}]}, {"id": "FAM:SF18", "label": "Study family SF18: Fragility confirmatory: F1a usage decoupling and F1b split-half stability of residual influence", "score": 0.351, "reached_via": ["request matches METH:split_half_reliability (0.32); FAM:SF18 auto_uses_method METH:split_half_reliability", "request matches RISK:MEASURE_RELIABILITY (0.32); FAM:SF18 auto_has_risk RISK:MEASURE_RELIABILITY"], "attributes": {"observed_research_question": "Fragility confirmatory: F1a usage decoupling and F1b split-half stability of residual influence", "auto_outcome_status": "supported", "observed_hypothesis": "Structural influence is not reducible to usage and the usage-residual is a reproducible player property.", "observed_result": ["[APPA-039] F1a cosine R2=0.094, residual-share=0.906, CI [0.768, 0.962] PASS; Frobenius R2=0.073 share=0.927 CI [0.828, 0.965]. F1b pooled-residual rho=+0.685 p=0.0000 CI [+0.649, +0.721]; usage-partial rho=+0.557 p=0.00 [cut; read_family for the full text]", "[APPS-083] F1a cosine R2=0.099 share=0.901 CI[0.778,0.954]; frobenius R2=0.084 share=0.916. F1b pooled rho=+0.670 p=0.0000 CI[+0.636,+0.705]; partial rho=+0.560 CI[+0.496,+0.616]. F1a=CONFIRMED F1b=CONFIRMED."], "auto_failure_mechanism": "D_positive (no failure: positive result)"}, "relationships": [{"rel": "auto_limited_by", "node": "LIM:low_measurement_reliability"}, {"rel": "auto_has_risk", "node": "RISK:MEASURE_RELIABILITY"}]}], "n_results": 4}

